Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the **Glenarrow Town Centre** conservation area. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs planning permission unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material (for example, timber to uPVC) or the design (for example, the glazing pattern or opening style), you will likely need to submit an application before starting work.

If you're unsure whether your proposal matches the existing windows closely enough, I'd suggest contacting the planning desk before you order anything. I can't give a formal opinion on your specific proposal, but the council can advise on whether an application is needed.
